  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ AVC_FAITH IS FREEDOM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Violence against women is a major issue in my community. Through this project, the community will be empowered about gender equality and harmful prejudices that limit women&apos;s rights based on religious faith. AVC will execute a community awareness campaign to reach out to project beneficiaries in order to reach a targeted community and solve the barrier. AVC has partnered with Art Group in Dares Salaam to collaborate on the campaign. The art group will perform numerous dramas that will offer various messages to educate the community about women&apos;s rights, stop stereotypes that violate women&apos;s rights, and promote equality. We will distribute posters, leaflets, and magazines to the assembled crowd with messages about gender equality. Furthermore, AVC will hold workshops in each community to educate men and women about gender equality and to combat the stereotypes that contribute to GBV. Participants will include members of the community (including men and women), village officials, and religious leaders. Professional facilitators on GBV and human rights will be involved. Religious leaders will provide information on how to stop the violation of the stereotype of women.


The participative method will be employed in the workshops and training to ensure that project participants act as agents and front-line ambassadors in raising knowledge of their rights. Some of our team members have been victims of Gender Based Violence (GBV), and they will work together to achieve the project&apos;s objectives. In addition,village leaders and victims of GBV from the targeted community will attend the workshops to share their experiences and educate other participants. The project &#xA0;aims to prepare beneficiaries to positively contribute to their community in order to reduce the harmful stereotypes that create GBV and other forms of violencethat are destructive to the community.

The project will educate women about their human rights potential: Women and other community members will gain necessary knowledge and skills about women&apos;s rights as a result of raising awareness, and harmful stereotypes that encourage gender inequity and violence will be eliminated. In addition, the project will minimize Gender Based Violence (GBV) in the targeted community in the long run: The project will force GBV to leave the Kisarawe region, where the difficulty is quite great. The community will be aware of the negative attitudes toward women and will use faith as a tool to protect them from various formsof assault.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afri-Tanzania Volunteers for Change is a Volunteer Organization started working since January 2013 and registered with registrationnumber 00NGO/00007623 under the Ministry of Community Development, Gender and Children in Tanzania. It deals with facilitating youth (locally and internationally) to volunteer to the society by giving a helping hand in every way they can.

Afri-Tanzania Volunteers for Change (AVC) is a highly recommended not-for-profit in Dar es Salaam, Tanzania. They offer a variety of volunteer opportunities including teaching, marketing and advertising, volunteering in an orphanage and working with human right issues. These projects include the following:

Teaching and Education:
Volunteers can teach English, Physics, Biology and Math at Kibwegele and Kibamba secondary schools, teach English at Mloganzila and Kibamba primary schools and Teaching English and crafts(Drawings) at Nursery schools both located in our host communities. Our schools face a shortage of teachers.

Orphanage Centers:
Volunteers may work with children in &#x201C;New Life Orphans Home&#x201D; located at Tegeta and &#x201C;Child and Son Center&#x201D; at Mbezi both in Dar es salaam Region 10-20 km from AVC office. Teach English, Math or health lessons to children, washing clothes, Organize sporting events for orphans to improve their socialskills and other duties volunteers want to arrange. The volunteers can live at special Rooms within the centers.

Capacity Building, Awareness and Advocacy.
Support by run projects based on Children, women and disabled Rights, Reproductive health, Environmental conservation, entrepreneurship education, and drug abuse to primary and secondary school students and youths Groups in Kinondoni District of Dar es salaam and Kisarawe District of Pwani Region. The beneficiaries are youth between ages 7 to 24. This project aim to create youth to be good future generation and leader for providing soft skills and awareness needed to them to ensure they know them self and have self determination.

Advertising and Fundraising Opportunities:
Volunteers can help AVC expand virally throughout the world by advertising the organization. Furthermore, volunteers can help write grant proposals, Funds or Fundraising to support our programmes, collect used and new tools, School books, clothes and other equipment like computers and anything from their home countries to donate in order to support poor children and orphans lives in rural communities and AVC projects.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afri-Tanzania Volunteers for Change</narrative>
